I can't access the MCP configuration files due to security restrictions that limit file access to the current working directory (`/Users/rorikurniadi/code/smb-app/ide-phoenix`).

To view your GitLab MCP configuration, you'll need to check:

**macOS locations:**
```bash
# Claude Desktop MCP settings
~/.config/claude-desktop/mcp_settings.json
# or
~/Library/Application Support/Claude/mcp_settings.json

# Claude Desktop configuration
~/.config/claude-desktop/config.json
```

**Common GitLab MCP configuration structure:**
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "gitlab": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": [
        "@modelcontextprotocol/server-gitlab"
      ],
      "env": {
        "GITLAB_URL": "https://your-gitlab-instance.com",
        "GITLAB_CLIENT_ID": "your-oauth-client-id",
        "GITLAB_CLIENT_SECRET": "your-oauth-client-secret"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Please check these files manually to see your current GitLab MCP configuration.
